{
  "id": "19085_kaitou",
  "headword": "{解凍|かいとう}",
  "reading": "かいとう",
  "romaji": "kaitou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "thawing; defrosting; decompression",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "thawing; defrosting",
      "explanation": "The process of bringing frozen food or substances back to a non-frozen state."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "decompression; unzipping; extracting",
      "explanation": "In computing, the process of extracting compressed files back to their original state."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{冷凍|れいとう}{肉|にく}を{解凍|かいとう}する。",
      "english": "To thaw frozen meat.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{電子|でんし}レンジで{解凍|かいとう}すると{早|はや}い。",
      "english": "Defrosting in the microwave is fast.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{自然|しぜん}{解凍|かいとう}の{方|ほう}が{味|あじ}が{落|お}ちにくい。",
      "english": "Natural thawing is less likely to affect the flavor.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex4",
      "japanese": "ファイルを{解凍|かいとう}する。",
      "english": "To unzip a file.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex5",
      "japanese": "ダウンロードした{圧縮|あっしゅく}ファイルを{解凍|かいとう}してください。",
      "english": "Please extract the compressed file you downloaded.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "19085_kaitou_ex6",
      "japanese": "{解凍|かいとう}ソフトをインストールしないと、このファイルは{開|ひら}けない。",
      "english": "You can't open this file without installing decompression software.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The food sense is the original meaning, while the computing sense is a metaphorical extension. For food, common methods include {自然|しぜん}{解凍|かいとう} (natural thawing at room temperature), {流水|りゅうすい}{解凍|かいとう} (thawing under running water), and {電子|でんし}レンジ{解凍|かいとう} (microwave defrosting). The opposite is {冷凍|れいとう} (freezing) for food and {圧縮|あっしゅく} (compression) for files. This is a する verb: {解凍|かいとう}する.",
